## 5. Run identity section **[UPDATED — layout + inline confound badges]**

**What it shows:** One card per uploaded run (was a fixed 2-column grid in v1; now wraps to fit N).

**What it means:** Same purpose as v1 — confirm what you're comparing before trusting the numbers — but two changes: the grid is no longer hardcoded to 2 columns, and anything that used to live in the old fixed "2 data validity notes" banner (§ removed, see Section 8 below) now attaches directly to the specific run card it's about.

| # | Field | Detail |
|---|---|---|
| 5.1 | Grid layout | `repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr))` behavior — 2 runs = 2 columns (as in v1), 4 runs = 2×2 or 4×1 depending on width, 8+ runs = wraps to multiple rows. Top border color = that run's palette color from §0. |
| 5.2 | Card fields (unchanged from v1) | Session ID, prompt length, working dir, turns, tool calls |
| 5.3 | **[NEW] Inline confound badge** | A small warning icon in the card's top-right corner, shown *only* if this specific run has a flagged data-quality issue (e.g., resent prompt, rejected tool call). Click/tap reveals the note inline (expands under the card fields) — nothing is shown if the run has no issues. This is what replaces the fixed banner from v1. |

