## 6. Dynamic KPI section **[UPDATED — was fixed 4 cards, now variable 0–N]**

**What it shows:** Headline cards, but now generated from what actually drifted rather than a fixed set of four.

**What it means:** Every computed metric gets a drift-severity classification first (no drift / moderate / large / categorical / cannot-determine / uninterpretable). Only metrics above "no drift" become KPI cards here, ranked by how large the drift is. This section can be empty, small, or larger depending on the comparison — it is not a fixed 4-up grid anymore.

| # | State | Behavior |
|---|---|---|
| 6.1 | Metrics with drift found (typical case) | One card per qualifying metric, ranked highest-drift-first, same card anatomy as v1 (value(s), verdict chip) but value display adapts to N: 2 runs show "A vs B" as in v1; 3+ runs show the group range plus the outlier run's value, e.g. **"4,920 – 12,044 (Run 3 highest)"**. |
| 6.2 | Cap on visible cards | Show at most 6 by default; if more than 6 metrics qualify, show the top 6 and a **"+3 more drifted metrics — view full table"** link rather than growing the row indefinitely. |
| 6.3 | **[NEW] Empty state** | If zero metrics clear the drift threshold across all loaded runs: replace the entire KPI row with a single centered message: *"No metric shows meaningful drift across these N runs."* — not an empty grid, not hidden entirely (its absence would look like a loading bug). |
| 6.4 | Per-card content, unchanged from v1 | Label, value(s), verdict chip using the same signal colors as §0 |

