## 7. Charts **[UPDATED — multi-run rendering + large-N fallback]**

Same four charts as v1, each needing to support more than two series.

### 7.1 Cache-creation intensity (grouped bars)
- 2–4 runs: same paired/grouped horizontal bars as v1, one bar per run per row, colored per §0's palette.
- 5+ runs: switch to a **strip plot** per row instead (one dot per run along a single horizontal scale, so the row height doesn't grow linearly with run count) — see 7.6 for the general threshold rule.

### 7.2 Overhead-ratio trend (line chart)
- One line per run instead of a fixed two; legend below lists every run's growth multiple (e.g. "Run 1 — 10.4x", "Run 2 — 7.4x", "Run 3 — 6.1x"), sorted steepest-first.
- Beyond ~6 runs, fade non-outlier lines to 30% opacity and keep the highest/lowest growth lines at full opacity, so the chart stays readable — outliers are what matters most here.

### 7.3 Tool usage by type
- Same per-tool-name row layout as v1, bar count per row scales with N runs the same way as 7.1.
- The v1 behavior of flagging a categorically-different row (a tool used by only one run, like `mcp_tool`) generalizes to: flag any row where at least one run has zero and at least one run has a non-zero count.

### 7.4 Where the wall-clock time went
- Same three-bars-per-run (Active / Permission-wait / Other idle) as v1, one group per run — stacks vertically as N grows rather than assuming exactly two groups.

### 7.5 **[NEW] Aggregate/distribution view toggle**
When N is large enough that per-run color coding stops being legible, each chart above gets a small toggle: **"Per-run" / "Distribution"**. Distribution mode replaces individual bars/lines with a box-and-whisker or strip plot per metric (median line, interquartile range, outlier points labeled with their run). *(The exact N threshold for defaulting to Distribution mode is an open question — see the spec doc's Open Questions. Suggested starting default: 6.)*

### 7.6 General rule this section encodes
> Any chart with per-run series must define what happens as N grows — this document sets a soft default of switching emphasis (not necessarily hiding data) somewhere around 5–6 runs; the exact number is intentionally left as a tunable, not hardcoded here.

