## 10. Full comparison table **[UPDATED — dynamic columns]**

**What it shows:** Same row-per-metric structure as v1, but the column set is generated from the runs loaded instead of fixed "Detailed / Generic" columns.

| # | Change |
|---|---|
| 10.1 | Columns become: Metric \| Run 1 \| Run 2 \| … \| Run N \| Spread \| Signal. Run column headers use each run's short label + color swatch from §0. |
| 10.2 | **[NEW] "Spread" column** — replaces v1's single "Diff" column when N>2 (for N=2 it can still just show the simple diff, as in v1). For N>2, shows the range or coefficient of variation across runs at a glance, before the reader even looks at individual values. |
| 10.3 | Signal column | Unchanged meaning from v1 (No drift / Moderate / Large / Categorical / Uninterpretable / Cannot determine), computed across all N runs rather than just a pairwise diff. |
| 10.4 | Wide-table handling | With enough runs, the table scrolls horizontally within its own card (frozen Metric column), rather than the whole page scrolling sideways. |

